claims:
1. A medical system comprising:
a set of log files, wherein each log file contains informa- tion on the use and/or performance of the medical system or a component thereof;
a log file uploader comprising an upload configuration component that determines what log files to upload to a remote service engineer and a log file uploader that uploads one or more log files based on an upload configuration determined by the upload configuration component;
at least one user input device; and
at least one electronic processor programmed to:
receive input via the user input device from a parts ordering system for ordering replacement parts for medical systems identifying a potential replacement part by a part-type-number (PTN);
wherein the input is a PTN of a part identified by the parts ordering system as a part related to a part that has been recently ordered for replacement;
determine one or more logging metrics within the medical system log files that correspond to the entered PTN;
extract the determined one or more logging metrics into a new medical system log file; and
instruct the upload configuration component to modify the log file upload configuration to include and prioritize the upload of the new log file.
2. The medical system of claim 1, wherein the newly created log file includes an identification tag.
3. The medical system of claim 2, wherein the identifi- cation tag includes information related to a priority, an identification history, and/or a criticality of the part for which the newly create log file was created.
4. The medical system of claim 1, wherein the processor is further configured to send information to the parts order- ing system related to a date in which the part of the monitored PTN was replaced.
5. The medical system of claim 1, wherein the identifi- cation of the PTN of the part includes:
querying a list of possible extracted parts against a log file of a medical device associated with the part ordered via the parts ordering system to identify the extracted part.
6. The medical system of claim 1, wherein the medical system comprises a medical imaging device or a patient monitor.
